WEBVTT

01:05.125 --> 01:08.262
Are you here for the blind date?

01:10.065 --> 01:12.317
Oh, that's not me.

01:12.317 --> 01:13.402
Sorry about that.

01:13.402 --> 01:14.426
Ui Yeong!

01:14.426 --> 01:16.369
- You're here?
- Over here!

01:16.369 --> 01:17.526
It's been forever.

01:17.526 --> 01:19.417
- You look stunning today.
- Seriously.

01:19.417 --> 01:20.284
- You think?
- Yeah.

01:20.284 --> 01:22.619
- It's your day.
- You're glowing!

01:22.619 --> 01:24.453
Thank you.

01:24.453 --> 01:25.548
How've you been?

01:25.548 --> 01:27.500
- Yeah, it's been a while.
- Right?

01:27.500 --> 01:30.000
- We only see each other like this.
- It takes a wedding invite

01:30.000 --> 01:32.876
- to get us together.
- Exactly.

01:32.876 --> 01:35.164
Everything good with you?

01:36.542 --> 01:38.709
Thank you.

01:39.980 --> 01:41.013
Fancy.

01:41.013 --> 01:42.584
- Good?
- Yeah.

01:42.584 --> 01:45.976
- It looks great, so clean.
- I really tried.

01:45.976 --> 01:49.521
[We would be grateful for your warm wishes]
- You're actually getting married. - Seriously.

01:49.521 --> 01:52.492
Feels like you just booked the venue.
Time flies, right?

01:52.492 --> 01:54.452
- I know.
- Congrats.

01:54.452 --> 01:55.632
You must be swamped.

01:55.632 --> 01:58.032
I have zero free time.
Planning a gathering to hand out invitations,

01:58.032 --> 02:00.251
sorting out the program, and moving...

02:00.251 --> 02:03.240
Next week, I've got a wedding checkup.

02:03.240 --> 02:04.328
Wedding checkup?

02:04.328 --> 02:07.998
It just sounds fancy.
It's a fertility screening.

02:07.998 --> 02:10.667
OB-GYN, urology.

02:10.667 --> 02:13.209
People do that now?

02:13.209 --> 02:16.006
But sometimes it's actually fun.

02:16.006 --> 02:17.358
Like what?

02:19.301 --> 02:21.261
- No way!
- It's gorgeous!

02:21.261 --> 02:22.408
So pretty!

02:22.408 --> 02:24.375
See how it shines.

02:24.375 --> 02:27.684
- Unbelievable.
- Ui Yeong was bored until she saw the ring.

02:27.684 --> 02:28.685
Exactly.

02:28.685 --> 02:31.438
It's massive.
I've never seen anything this big.

02:31.438 --> 02:32.606
Doesn't it weigh a ton?

02:32.606 --> 02:33.927
- It really does.
- Right?

02:33.927 --> 02:35.292
- Put it down.
- Oh, stop.

02:35.292 --> 02:37.327
Seriously.

02:37.327 --> 02:39.071
Ui Yeong, aren't you getting married?

02:39.071 --> 02:40.155
Me?

02:40.155 --> 02:42.699
Once I'm gone, you're the last single one.

02:42.699 --> 02:45.202
Oh... I guess so?

02:45.202 --> 02:49.664
Is your boyfriend not exactly
marriage material?

02:49.664 --> 02:52.542
No, he's a really good guy.

02:52.542 --> 02:54.976
I just don't want to get married yet.

02:55.962 --> 02:58.548
But for you guys,

02:58.548 --> 03:02.668
was there a moment you just knew?

03:03.261 --> 03:05.769
While we were eating together,

03:05.769 --> 03:09.667
I thought we would eat like this forever.

03:09.667 --> 03:10.727
And you?

03:10.727 --> 03:13.438
When I got pregnant.

03:13.438 --> 03:17.292
He took charge and explained it to my parents.

03:17.292 --> 03:19.750
It made me trust him.

03:19.750 --> 03:21.625
Do I have to think about all that?

03:21.625 --> 03:23.167
If you meet someone at this age,

03:23.167 --> 03:25.992
shouldn't you just get married?

03:25.992 --> 03:27.481
Bring your boyfriend to the wedding.

03:27.481 --> 03:29.292
We'll evaluate him.

03:29.292 --> 03:32.083
I'm curious.

03:32.083 --> 03:36.002
Okay, I'll ask if he has time.

03:36.002 --> 03:37.754
Oh, right.

03:37.754 --> 03:39.089
- Ui Yeong.
- Yeah.

03:39.089 --> 03:41.919
- Could you give a speech at our wedding?
- Me?

03:41.919 --> 03:44.208
- Hey, I can't do that.
- Why?

03:44.208 --> 03:47.139
- You've always been good at speaking.
- Yeah.

03:47.139 --> 03:50.809
I only did that to get good grades.

03:50.809 --> 03:53.478
- I don't know anything about marriage.
- Hey.

03:53.478 --> 03:56.417
I hate the idea of me
trembling in front of the speaker

03:56.417 --> 03:58.650
and tearing up before even hearing the speech.

03:58.650 --> 04:00.399
I seriously can't stand that kind of thing.

04:00.399 --> 04:01.750
I really can't do it.

04:01.750 --> 04:04.657
Just do it comfortably and casually.

04:04.657 --> 04:06.117
- Right.
- Just say nice things.

04:06.117 --> 04:08.410
- Please do it.
- Yeah, just do it.

04:08.410 --> 04:11.204
- Eun Mi wants it so much.
- Yeah.

04:11.204 --> 04:12.500
Okay.

04:12.500 --> 04:14.250
Really?

04:14.250 --> 04:16.500
Yeah! I got someone!

04:16.500 --> 04:17.657
You said keep it casual.

04:17.657 --> 04:19.167
- Yeah, just keep it casual.
- Okay.

04:19.167 --> 04:20.296
[Episode 12]
Don't cry, you guys.

04:20.296 --> 04:22.572
You shouldn't cry either.

04:23.716 --> 04:27.026
How do you want to remodel your workspace?

04:27.709 --> 04:30.458
Some customers want to buy in person.

04:30.458 --> 04:33.709
I want to add a small showroom to the space.

04:33.709 --> 04:35.961
Because it's so small.

04:35.961 --> 04:38.082
Can I take some pictures?

04:38.082 --> 04:39.393
Oh, yes.

04:39.393 --> 04:42.292
If we add upper cabinets for storage,

04:42.292 --> 04:44.195
- the space will be fine.
- Oh, okay.

04:44.195 --> 04:46.505
Do you have a design in mind?

04:46.505 --> 04:48.000
Actually,

04:48.000 --> 04:51.709
I saw your chair at the exhibit and hired you.

04:51.709 --> 04:54.748
I like designs that don't go out of style.

04:54.748 --> 04:56.134
I like that kind of design.

04:56.134 --> 04:57.459
Yes, I understand.

04:57.459 --> 04:59.326
Thank you.

05:00.153 --> 05:02.974
Did you make this yourself too?

05:02.974 --> 05:04.774
Oh, yes.

05:06.750 --> 05:09.718
These are beautiful.

05:10.834 --> 05:12.250
Wearing a ring like this,

05:12.250 --> 05:15.041
doesn't it make you fall in love?

05:15.041 --> 05:17.292
You think so? Maybe that's why.

05:17.292 --> 05:19.856
Every couple who wore them got married.

05:19.856 --> 05:20.895
Really?

05:20.895 --> 05:22.333
Yes.

05:22.333 --> 05:24.194
But I don't want to break that reputation.

05:24.194 --> 05:25.792
So I'm stopping here.

05:25.792 --> 05:28.323
I'm only making custom rings from now on.

05:28.323 --> 05:30.899
Oh, okay.

05:31.951 --> 05:33.730
Shall I show you the inside too?

05:33.730 --> 05:35.530
Yes.

05:39.793 --> 05:42.379
[Ho Jin and Eun Mi are tying the knot.
We'd be honored if you'd share in their joy]

05:48.851 --> 05:50.554
Ui Yeong.

05:50.554 --> 05:52.547
Are you here?

05:52.547 --> 05:53.592
I bet you're starving.

05:53.592 --> 05:55.683
I hardly touched my food to save room for you.

05:55.683 --> 05:57.190
Barely anything.

05:57.190 --> 05:58.228
Smart move.

05:58.228 --> 06:00.500
- I'm so hungry.
- Let's grab some food.

06:00.500 --> 06:02.806
That looks delicious.

06:08.500 --> 06:10.481
Looks incredible.

06:15.417 --> 06:16.452
Here, have this one.

06:16.452 --> 06:18.572
Oh, thank you.

06:22.196 --> 06:23.577
This looks amazing.

06:23.577 --> 06:25.454
Go ahead, try it.

06:32.417 --> 06:33.677
The sauce is incredible.

06:33.677 --> 06:35.116
- Right?
- Yeah.

06:35.116 --> 06:38.709
Your restaurant picks never disappoint.

06:38.709 --> 06:40.316
Right.

06:40.316 --> 06:43.496
This is instant happiness in a bite.

06:43.496 --> 06:46.272
So, how was seeing your friends?

06:47.276 --> 06:49.381
We talked nonstop.

06:49.381 --> 06:52.362
And my friends are dying to meet you.

06:52.362 --> 06:54.015
They want me to bring you to a wedding.

06:54.015 --> 06:55.876
Let's go. I'll make time.

06:55.876 --> 06:57.945
- Really?
- Yeah.

06:58.958 --> 07:03.041
Weekends are nothing but showers or weddings.

07:03.041 --> 07:05.622
We only get to date in our spare time

07:05.622 --> 07:08.038
because I'm busy celebrating others.

07:09.625 --> 07:11.250
Tae Seop,

07:11.250 --> 07:12.759
do people around you

07:12.759 --> 07:15.164
talk about marriage a lot?

07:16.250 --> 07:17.682
I guess so.

07:17.682 --> 07:20.631
Before, it was mostly about who works where

07:20.631 --> 07:22.250
or who makes how much.

07:22.250 --> 07:24.307
That was what we mostly talked about.

07:24.307 --> 07:26.625
Now it's all weddings and apartments.

07:26.625 --> 07:28.767
The whole conversation's shifted.

07:29.528 --> 07:33.390
Everyone is naturally moving on to that phase.

07:33.390 --> 07:35.366
It might be natural for some,

07:35.366 --> 07:37.536
but it might still be unfamiliar to others.

07:37.536 --> 07:40.150
I think everyone has their own pace.

07:40.150 --> 07:41.950
Right.

07:42.909 --> 07:44.050
Are you free tomorrow?

07:44.050 --> 07:45.709
I was thinking of bringing the chair.

07:45.709 --> 07:48.989
Really? It's finally coming!

07:48.989 --> 07:51.808
I love it. I can't wait to sit in it.

07:51.808 --> 07:54.610
- I'll bring it tomorrow.
- Sounds great.

08:03.834 --> 08:05.754
- No, wait.
- What?

08:05.754 --> 08:08.530
You really can't do this. This is Mom's trophy.

08:08.530 --> 08:10.350
It isn't a trophy. It's whiskey.

08:10.350 --> 08:11.449
No.

08:11.449 --> 08:13.863
I got it from my team leader for exceeding

08:13.863 --> 08:16.866
- my goals by 100% for the first time.
- No.

08:16.866 --> 08:18.868
No, let's just leave this

08:18.868 --> 08:21.394
as a glory of my youth.

08:21.394 --> 08:22.944
Did you not hear what the doctor said?

08:22.944 --> 08:25.959
Why did you leave it sealed for so long?

08:25.959 --> 08:27.667
Mom, stop being like that.

08:27.667 --> 08:30.323
Let's have some tea instead of drinks.

08:30.323 --> 08:32.125
When I visited the tea fields,

08:32.125 --> 08:34.709
I learned the world of tea is super deep.

08:34.709 --> 08:36.064
White tea over white wine,

08:36.064 --> 08:38.125
and black tea instead of red wine.

08:38.125 --> 08:40.140
- Nonsense.
- Sounds good, right?

08:40.140 --> 08:42.375
- No more alcohol from now on?
- Today is definitely out of the question.

08:42.375 --> 08:44.551
You're speaking pure nonsense.

08:51.709 --> 08:53.453
It's incredibly comfortable.

08:53.453 --> 08:54.904
- Is it comfortable?
- Yeah, the back too.

08:54.904 --> 08:58.000
How did you make something like this?
It's good.

08:58.000 --> 08:59.425
I'm so glad.

08:59.425 --> 09:01.948
Doesn't it fit perfectly in our house?

09:01.948 --> 09:05.265
- Totally.
- Thank you.

09:05.265 --> 09:07.459
Grab some tea once you finish up.

09:07.459 --> 09:08.542
Yes.

09:08.542 --> 09:10.342
Let's go.

09:13.041 --> 09:15.248
Smells amazing.

09:15.834 --> 09:17.408
Is it to your liking?

09:17.408 --> 09:19.726
I'm really enjoying it.

09:22.306 --> 09:26.017
So do you craft furniture like that
for a living?

09:26.017 --> 09:27.500
Yes, I make furniture,

09:27.500 --> 09:30.064
and I also design entire spaces for brands

09:30.064 --> 09:33.709
and architectural firms.

09:33.709 --> 09:35.657
Then you're definitely not a player.

09:35.657 --> 09:37.212
- Mom.
- What?

09:37.948 --> 09:39.542
Nothing.

09:39.542 --> 09:41.321
Do you have a life goal?

09:41.321 --> 09:43.202
Mom, why would you even ask that?

09:43.202 --> 09:44.881
Do you have a goal, Mom?

09:44.881 --> 09:46.802
I just live day by day now.

09:46.802 --> 09:48.124
But I had one at your age.

09:48.124 --> 09:51.336
It was to support you until college.

09:53.087 --> 09:54.375
Until my twenties,

09:54.375 --> 09:57.781
I wanted to prove myself through work.

09:57.781 --> 09:59.260
But these days, rather than work,

09:59.260 --> 10:01.125
I love spending time with Ui Yeong,

10:01.125 --> 10:03.842
my family, and my colleagues.

10:03.842 --> 10:05.480
It feels like I'm truly living.

10:05.480 --> 10:08.478
Going a long way together
with the people around me

10:08.478 --> 10:11.333
is my goal, if I had to name one.

10:11.333 --> 10:13.917
You know what matters.

10:13.917 --> 10:17.722
- Last thing, and I'm most curious about this.
- Oh, Mom.

10:17.722 --> 10:21.399
- Please stop asking questions.
- What do you like so much about our Ui Yeong?

10:21.399 --> 10:24.192
I'm a little curious too.

10:26.000 --> 10:27.497
At first, because she's beautiful.

10:27.497 --> 10:29.179
Hear that?

10:29.179 --> 10:31.375
We clicked right away talking.

10:31.375 --> 10:34.140
After getting to know her better, her honesty?

10:34.140 --> 10:36.041
Her unpredictable personality?

10:36.041 --> 10:39.333
Those things appealed to me.

10:39.333 --> 10:43.125
I'm calm and rational,
but when I'm with Ui Yeong,

10:43.125 --> 10:46.709
I become very active and emotional.

10:46.709 --> 10:50.041
I think maybe that's...

10:50.041 --> 10:51.887
what love is.

10:52.972 --> 10:54.876
I'm sorry.

10:54.876 --> 10:57.517
I learned a thing or two about love.

10:59.488 --> 11:02.324
You're shy after speaking so well.

11:02.324 --> 11:05.375
Your face looks like an apple.

11:05.375 --> 11:06.993
Oh, it's hot.

11:06.993 --> 11:08.292
I need to use the restroom...

11:08.292 --> 11:10.280
- Oh my.
- Over there.

11:12.433 --> 11:14.375
- Isn't he cute?
- Love.

11:14.375 --> 11:16.754
- Love.
- I'm being loved.

11:16.754 --> 11:17.839
He's cute.

11:17.839 --> 11:20.082
- Are you jealous?
- Yeah.

11:21.375 --> 11:23.293
Let me get the lights.

11:27.015 --> 11:29.083
Let's take a look.

11:29.083 --> 11:32.429
First, the bell peppers.

11:32.429 --> 11:34.229
Some sweet potatoes.

11:35.750 --> 11:38.793
And three tomatoes.

11:40.737 --> 11:44.876
Three nice sweet potatoes.

11:44.876 --> 11:47.889
Three potatoes as well.

11:47.889 --> 11:49.389
Hold on.

11:49.389 --> 11:51.709
You don't need to do that.

11:51.709 --> 11:52.750
You should eat more.

11:52.750 --> 11:55.528
You're a lot bigger than I am.

11:55.528 --> 11:57.712
We paid fifty-fifty.

11:57.712 --> 11:59.755
It's fine.

11:59.755 --> 12:03.329
They'll spoil before I finish them.

12:03.329 --> 12:05.428
I don't want to end up tossing them.

12:05.428 --> 12:07.180
It's better if you eat them up.

12:07.180 --> 12:10.249
I already bought my portion for half off.

12:10.249 --> 12:13.958
This makes more sense than splitting it.

12:13.958 --> 12:17.000
You're so sweet.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.834
Then,

12:18.834 --> 12:21.958
since you like these,

12:21.958 --> 12:23.937
three for you.

12:25.448 --> 12:28.952
You caught onto my preferences so quickly.

12:34.415 --> 12:36.000
[Building Owner]

12:37.793 --> 12:39.619
What's wrong?

12:40.421 --> 12:41.917
Just a moment.

12:41.917 --> 12:44.057
Sure.

12:44.057 --> 12:45.785
Hello, sir.

12:45.785 --> 12:47.794
This is Lim Seung Jun.

12:49.292 --> 12:51.328
Excuse me?

12:51.328 --> 12:53.690
[Total Operating Costs]

12:54.625 --> 12:57.188
How can they raise the rent again?

12:57.188 --> 13:00.692
I can't just turn off the climate control.

13:00.692 --> 13:03.292
Maybe I should sell a piece of equipment.

13:03.292 --> 13:05.446
If you keep selling things off
whenever this comes up,

13:05.446 --> 13:07.752
there won't be anything left in the gym.

13:07.752 --> 13:09.450
Let me take a look.

13:09.450 --> 13:10.958
[Total Fixed Costs,
Estimated Total Variable Costs]

13:10.958 --> 13:16.252
Maybe a first-floor gym was a stretch.

13:16.252 --> 13:19.784
I should've just gone for a basement.

13:23.430 --> 13:26.917
There's nothing left to cut back on.

13:27.876 --> 13:30.337
What if you move now?

13:31.542 --> 13:36.150
Then the renovation costs are just wasted,

13:36.150 --> 13:39.888
and members might not come along.

13:57.620 --> 13:59.261
Actually, there's one option.

13:59.261 --> 14:00.876
Yeah?

14:00.876 --> 14:02.680
- That'll fix it?
- Yeah.

14:02.680 --> 14:04.089
This apartment.

14:04.089 --> 14:07.874
Let go of this place and live with me.

14:09.010 --> 14:10.810
Seung Jun.

14:14.584 --> 14:17.133
Will you move in with me?

14:31.402 --> 14:32.905
Mom, you're still up?

14:32.905 --> 14:33.923
Oh, well...

14:33.923 --> 14:35.502
What are you holding?

14:35.502 --> 14:37.163
You're not about to work, are you?

14:37.163 --> 14:39.202
You can't overdo it.

14:39.202 --> 14:41.584
No, it's not that, I...

14:41.584 --> 14:43.044
Can you sit down for a second?

14:43.044 --> 14:44.911
Sure.

14:56.724 --> 14:59.656
[Divorce Consent Confirmation Form]

15:01.372 --> 15:04.149
One of my clients once said

15:04.149 --> 15:05.951
that experiencing hardship

15:05.951 --> 15:08.652
isn't necessarily the worst thing.

15:08.652 --> 15:12.193
I didn't get it back then,

15:12.193 --> 15:14.617
but now I think I understand.

15:14.617 --> 15:16.208
Things become so much clearer,

15:16.208 --> 15:20.041
what to hold onto and what to leave.

15:20.041 --> 15:21.948
So,

15:23.500 --> 15:25.667
if you're okay with it,

15:25.667 --> 15:27.620
I want to go through with this.

15:30.625 --> 15:32.667
Mom.

15:32.667 --> 15:34.208
This is your life.

15:34.208 --> 15:37.672
If you feel right about it, then go ahead.

15:38.292 --> 15:40.895
I won't be the daughter who stands in your way.

15:40.895 --> 15:43.386
I'll be the one cheering you on.

15:44.215 --> 15:46.389
Starting today,

15:47.333 --> 15:49.292
and every day after,

15:49.292 --> 15:51.834
I want you to live putting yourself

15:51.834 --> 15:54.698
before anyone else.

15:54.698 --> 15:58.485
If you can do that,
it'll make me genuinely happy too.

16:00.876 --> 16:03.084
Since

16:03.084 --> 16:06.242
when did you become this grown-up?

16:07.000 --> 16:09.448
That's all you, Mom.

16:10.083 --> 16:12.582
Oh, come on.

16:14.041 --> 16:16.936
- Okay. Let's do this.
- Yeah.

16:18.347 --> 16:19.849
[Divorce Consent Confirmation Form]

16:19.849 --> 16:23.185
[Park Jeong Im]

16:23.185 --> 16:28.473
[Divorce Consent Confirmation Form]

16:42.234 --> 16:44.347
Sae Byeok, check this out.

16:44.347 --> 16:47.083
He's a really good buddy of mine.

16:47.083 --> 16:49.083
Good-looking, right?

16:49.083 --> 16:51.173
Sweet guy too.

16:51.173 --> 16:52.314
How about it?

16:52.314 --> 16:54.249
Should I arrange a blind date?

16:55.876 --> 16:58.920
There he goes again, that idiot.

16:59.958 --> 17:02.975
Are you alright? I just heard a thud.

17:02.975 --> 17:03.995
- You're not hurt, are you?
- What did she just say?

17:03.995 --> 17:07.429
It's nothing, baby. I just got spooked...

17:10.274 --> 17:11.525
What's going on with you two?

17:11.525 --> 17:15.228
Oh boy, look what we've got here.

17:18.375 --> 17:20.640
Gosh.

17:20.640 --> 17:22.625
We all assumed you were like siblings,

17:22.625 --> 17:24.201
and it turns out there's a couple.

17:24.201 --> 17:26.457
I know, right? How cute.

17:26.457 --> 17:28.506
I thought you said you'd never
get involved with someone at work?

17:28.506 --> 17:32.208
Oh, I did say that. That was then.

17:32.208 --> 17:34.820
How long ago was that?

17:34.820 --> 17:36.860
The ink's barely dry.

17:36.860 --> 17:39.596
This is all your doing, sir.

17:40.432 --> 17:42.891
- What did I have to do with it?
- We owe it to you, sir.

17:42.891 --> 17:44.559
You kept leaving us behind

17:44.559 --> 17:46.715
to go meet your girlfriend.

17:46.715 --> 17:48.938
I've got something to take care of.
You guys go ahead.

17:48.938 --> 17:49.976
Nice work today.

17:49.976 --> 17:51.435
- Good work.
- Bye.

17:51.435 --> 17:53.892
So then...

17:54.860 --> 17:57.103
should the two of us just head out?

17:58.990 --> 18:01.274
- Careful, it's hot. Take your time.
- Okay.

18:04.792 --> 18:05.956
What's that you're doing?

18:05.956 --> 18:07.665
Ui Yeong showed me this trick.

18:07.665 --> 18:11.075
This way, you won't burn your mouth
and can eat faster.

18:15.333 --> 18:17.874
That appetite of yours.

18:18.801 --> 18:20.710
So cute.

18:22.834 --> 18:24.000
- Like this?
- Yeah.

18:29.917 --> 18:33.139
Oh, for this...

18:36.250 --> 18:39.792
If you balance it flat like this,
it stays still.

18:39.792 --> 18:41.689
Look. Not moving at all.

18:44.730 --> 18:47.070
That's really cool.

18:49.208 --> 18:53.190
We'll keep our relationship
from interfering with work.

18:53.190 --> 18:55.410
- Alright.
- You really believe you can manage that?

18:55.410 --> 18:58.709
But seriously,
you two are actually a perfect match.

18:58.709 --> 19:00.375
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

19:00.375 --> 19:02.810
At least now we don't have
to stress about being found out.

19:02.810 --> 19:06.375
We'll give it our all,
the hard parts included, together.

19:06.375 --> 19:07.770
Good.

19:07.770 --> 19:09.686
- How about matching couple rings?
- Why not?

19:09.686 --> 19:12.107
Couple rings? This soon?

19:12.107 --> 19:14.167
If we want them, we get them.
What's the big deal?

19:14.167 --> 19:17.247
Seriously, it hasn't even been that long.
Couple rings this fast?

19:17.247 --> 19:19.528
That's how it works now.

19:19.528 --> 19:23.186
Is this a workplace or a reality dating show?

19:23.186 --> 19:26.500
Oh, poor Bo Yoon's getting grumpy
about being the only single one.

19:26.500 --> 19:29.247
You're hardly one to talk, sir.

19:29.247 --> 19:30.747
You don't have anyone either.

19:30.747 --> 19:32.375
Me? Come on,

19:32.375 --> 19:34.377
what would you know?

19:34.377 --> 19:37.923
I have Sua.

19:37.923 --> 19:39.631
Hello, my little peanut.

19:39.631 --> 19:40.857
- Dad.
- Yeah.

19:40.857 --> 19:43.577
The power went out
so kindergarten's letting us go early today.

19:43.577 --> 19:44.917
Really? Should I come get you?

19:44.917 --> 19:46.807
No, take your time after work.

19:46.807 --> 19:48.397
I'm playing with Min Gyu.

19:48.397 --> 19:50.496
Min Gyu? Who is that?

19:50.496 --> 19:53.096
My boyfriend. Didn't I mention him?

19:53.096 --> 19:55.388
Boyfriend?

19:57.375 --> 19:59.526
Boyfriend or just a friend who's a boy...

19:59.526 --> 20:01.517
I told her to ask me before seeing anyone.

20:01.517 --> 20:05.148
Since when do kids
in kindergarten have boyfriends?

20:05.876 --> 20:08.994
Tae Seop and Jin Su are taken now...

20:08.994 --> 20:10.820
Sua!

20:11.990 --> 20:14.011
Oh, so you're Min Gyu.

20:14.011 --> 20:15.330
Hello.

20:15.330 --> 20:18.451
Well, at least my Sua's got good taste.

20:18.451 --> 20:20.455
Is it just the two of you?

20:21.117 --> 20:23.333
Mom!

20:45.125 --> 20:46.333
Yeah.

20:46.333 --> 20:47.699
- Mom.
- Yeah.

20:47.699 --> 20:50.370
- He gave me bubbles.
- Oh really?

20:50.370 --> 20:52.125
Did you thank him?

20:52.125 --> 20:53.917
Come on, say it.

20:53.917 --> 20:56.041
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

20:56.041 --> 20:57.066
Go play.

20:57.066 --> 20:59.211
He's got good manners.

20:59.211 --> 21:00.345
Thank you.

21:00.345 --> 21:02.458
Oh, it's nothing.

21:02.458 --> 21:04.466
But this is actually the first time

21:04.466 --> 21:07.625
I've heard of Min Gyu.

21:07.625 --> 21:09.555
My husband and I got divorced,

21:09.555 --> 21:12.799
and Min Gyu and I just moved here recently.

21:14.333 --> 21:16.886
My wife, she passed away.

21:20.292 --> 21:25.958
Min Gyu's on the timid side,
so I worried about whether he'd settle in.

21:25.958 --> 21:29.450
But he warmed up to Sua so quickly,
it really put my mind at ease.

21:29.450 --> 21:32.880
Sua's always had a way with other kids.

21:32.880 --> 21:35.458
We should get to know each other.

21:36.667 --> 21:38.721
Oh, yeah.

21:40.002 --> 21:41.920
They'll be playing for ages.

21:41.920 --> 21:45.000
How about we eat somewhere close by?

21:45.000 --> 21:47.667
Making dinner at home is such a pain anyway.

21:49.167 --> 21:50.750
Oh, yeah...

21:50.750 --> 21:52.432
I mean, that's true.

21:52.432 --> 21:54.424
Do you like

21:55.083 --> 21:56.343
kalguksu?

21:56.343 --> 21:57.479
Do you?

21:57.479 --> 21:59.404
Do you like it?

22:00.041 --> 22:01.841
Yeah.

22:02.500 --> 22:05.143
I think I'd like that.

22:28.634 --> 22:29.667
Hello.

22:29.667 --> 22:31.375
- Hey, you're here.
- Yeah.

22:31.375 --> 22:33.167
What's going on upstairs today?

22:33.167 --> 22:36.892
Ji Su's got a magazine interview
here at the cafe.

22:36.892 --> 22:38.064
That's great.

22:38.064 --> 22:39.364
You're welcome to order coffee.

22:39.364 --> 22:41.944
Two hot lattes to go, please.

22:41.944 --> 22:43.333
Sure.

22:43.333 --> 22:47.292
Should we head up and take a peek?

22:47.292 --> 22:48.544
Would that be alright?

22:48.544 --> 22:50.163
Absolutely.

22:50.163 --> 22:51.575
Shall we?

22:51.575 --> 22:54.143
You share a special bond with her, correct?

22:54.143 --> 22:57.945
Could you tell us something about Son Jeong A?

22:58.951 --> 23:01.458
Watching Son Jeong A work on set...

23:01.458 --> 23:03.151
she was remarkable.

23:03.151 --> 23:04.667
The concentration in her performance,

23:04.667 --> 23:06.311
the passion she has for the work...

23:06.311 --> 23:08.299
it all came through to me.

23:08.299 --> 23:09.967
- He's giving off that true actor vibe.
- I learned a lot.

23:09.967 --> 23:11.667
- If I get the chance...
- He sure does.

23:11.667 --> 23:15.000
I'd love to work with her again.

23:15.000 --> 23:16.208
Sure.

23:16.208 --> 23:20.218
What sort of actor
are you hoping to become from here?

23:35.667 --> 23:38.319
I don't know everything,

23:40.125 --> 23:43.458
but instead of trying so hard to avoid it,

23:43.458 --> 23:47.250
I hope you use that time and that energy

23:47.250 --> 23:50.540
to protect what you love.

23:53.041 --> 23:55.837
There must be something you care about too.

23:57.750 --> 24:02.102
A day, a month, and then a year.

24:02.102 --> 24:04.804
If you keep going like that,

24:05.458 --> 24:07.108
I'm sure there'll come a time

24:07.108 --> 24:10.142
when even this won't hurt so much anymore.

24:18.286 --> 24:20.920
A friend once said something to me.

24:22.331 --> 24:24.958
That she wished I'd hold on

24:24.958 --> 24:27.218
to what I really care about.

24:30.876 --> 24:34.183
When I took a quiet look within,

24:37.958 --> 24:40.815
what I really loved was acting.

24:41.917 --> 24:43.917
She shattered

24:43.917 --> 24:46.446
so many of my walls.

24:47.191 --> 24:50.150
For now, instead of choosing one path,

24:50.150 --> 24:54.245
I just want to chase whatever
makes my heart beat in each moment.

24:54.905 --> 24:57.375
- What an incredible thing to say.
- Ui Yeong, should we get going?

24:57.375 --> 24:59.250
Yeah, let's.

25:09.125 --> 25:12.458
So my next piece, I want it to be a romance.

25:12.458 --> 25:15.475
Something really warm and joyful.

25:16.218 --> 25:17.719
What I couldn't sort out in reality,

25:17.719 --> 25:20.618
I want to let it out
through my characters, no matter what.

25:20.618 --> 25:23.691
- I'll be cheering you on.
- Thank you.

25:30.834 --> 25:33.617
Ji Su's truly impressive.

25:33.617 --> 25:35.661
I know.

25:43.657 --> 25:45.372
If you all have time,

25:45.372 --> 25:47.798
how about an Eat Eat Club gathering
this weekend?

25:47.798 --> 25:49.537
- There's something I need to tell you all.
- Oh yes!

25:49.537 --> 25:51.417
I'm in.

25:51.417 --> 25:53.387
Sounds good.

25:58.051 --> 26:00.137
There's something I need to share with you.

26:00.137 --> 26:01.166
What?

26:01.166 --> 26:03.515
Seung Jun and I are going to live together.

26:03.515 --> 26:04.746
What?

26:04.746 --> 26:06.926
The two of you sharing a place...

26:06.926 --> 26:08.569
for real?

26:09.667 --> 26:11.834
He was agonizing over the gym rent,

26:11.834 --> 26:15.445
so I told him to just bring his toothbrush
and come on over.

26:15.445 --> 26:17.904
He spent a few days overthinking it,

26:17.904 --> 26:19.387
then said alright.

26:19.387 --> 26:21.458
Wait, hold on.

26:21.458 --> 26:23.243
Isn't that a bit soon?

26:23.243 --> 26:24.900
Aren't you going to feel weird about it?

26:24.900 --> 26:27.080
He gets in late at night

26:27.080 --> 26:29.040
and only uses the place to crash, so it's fine.

26:29.040 --> 26:32.426
And when it comes to sleeping together...

26:34.359 --> 26:35.839
we've always been compatible.

26:35.839 --> 26:37.454
Hey.

26:38.250 --> 26:41.000
Are you really sure about this?

26:41.000 --> 26:42.500
To be honest,

26:42.500 --> 26:44.975
I didn't agonize over the decision.

26:44.975 --> 26:47.269
I just felt sorry for him.

26:47.269 --> 26:49.686
It's not because he's the guy I'm dating.

26:49.686 --> 26:51.438
I've never met anyone who hustles this hard

26:51.438 --> 26:54.596
without relying on a single break.

26:54.596 --> 26:56.037
That does sound like him.

26:56.037 --> 26:58.314
In this unforgiving world,

26:58.314 --> 27:02.665
I want to at least be
Seung Jun's stroke of luck.

27:04.709 --> 27:07.236
You're different now.

27:07.236 --> 27:09.797
Should I call it more mature?

27:10.541 --> 27:13.001
Or more like an adult?

27:13.001 --> 27:15.177
- Really?
- Yeah.

27:16.880 --> 27:18.884
I mean, my figure's already grown up,

27:18.884 --> 27:22.141
and if my heart follows suit,
that's truly lethal.

27:22.141 --> 27:24.514
- Right?
- Come on.

27:24.514 --> 27:25.876
I'm withdrawing what I just said.

27:25.876 --> 27:27.857
Pretend it never happened.

27:29.667 --> 27:32.998
I should check
if Seung Jun can join the Eat Eat Club too.

27:32.998 --> 27:34.082
You're fine with that, right?

27:34.082 --> 27:35.905
Yeah. That's fine with me.

27:35.905 --> 27:38.565
Now that he's part of the household,
I need to look after his meals.

27:38.565 --> 27:39.965
Oh, starting already.

27:39.965 --> 27:42.824
Ui Yeong, come see me. I need a word.

27:42.824 --> 27:44.484
- Hyun Min, you too.
- Yes.

27:44.484 --> 27:46.459
Yes.

27:49.204 --> 27:51.541
- You know that fruit delivery from yesterday.
- Yeah.

27:51.541 --> 27:54.230
The sugar content is totally inconsistent.

27:54.230 --> 27:57.672
The kitchen's telling us
it's practically unusable.

27:57.672 --> 27:59.758
Every crate they crack open tastes different.

27:59.758 --> 28:01.087
How did you handle the vendors

28:01.087 --> 28:02.834
- while I was away?
- No...

28:02.834 --> 28:05.111
We checked it all when the delivery arrived.

28:05.111 --> 28:07.997
Well, if you checked it,
you should've done it properly.

28:07.997 --> 28:12.375
Were you just going through the motions?

28:12.375 --> 28:16.041
But if it arrived yesterday,
wouldn't that be K Produce?

28:16.041 --> 28:19.486
That was the one you...

28:19.486 --> 28:23.584
Please, just stop making excuses.

28:23.584 --> 28:25.992
Just do things properly.

28:25.992 --> 28:28.501
Where's Mrs. Na Ri?

28:33.999 --> 28:35.611
Sorry, I was held up going over some documents.

28:35.611 --> 28:37.891
- Regarding the kitchen complaint.
- Yeah,

28:37.891 --> 28:41.210
I was actually in the middle
of setting them straight on that.

28:41.210 --> 28:42.526
That supplier.

28:42.526 --> 28:44.787
You recommended them yourself, sir.

28:44.787 --> 28:46.720
And you ran the inspection solo.

28:46.720 --> 28:49.125
The vendor oversight falls on you, sir.

28:49.125 --> 28:52.746
So why are you blaming the staff?

28:52.746 --> 28:54.811
What?

28:54.811 --> 28:58.000
No, I didn't...

28:58.000 --> 28:59.906
[Inspection report by Oh Myeong Un]
Oh, right. That was me.

28:59.906 --> 29:03.000
Ui Yeong, sweetness testing was
a condition of the agreement,

29:03.000 --> 29:05.488
so send back everything that arrived

29:05.488 --> 29:07.240
and submit a fresh order.

29:07.240 --> 29:10.035
And make sure they understand that
if this kind of error occurs again,

29:10.035 --> 29:12.648
we'll end the partnership for good.

29:12.648 --> 29:15.625
Yes, got it.

29:15.625 --> 29:17.167
On another note.

29:17.167 --> 29:20.542
I heard you gave the green light right away

29:20.542 --> 29:22.659
when marketing proposed
pushing up the new menu release.

29:22.659 --> 29:23.715
We were planning to anyway...

29:23.715 --> 29:26.569
Wouldn't it make sense
to assess things internally

29:26.569 --> 29:28.908
before moving forward?

29:28.908 --> 29:32.182
We're not comfortable
with how this has been managed.

29:32.182 --> 29:33.516
While you were gone,

29:33.516 --> 29:35.894
we put in real effort to cover for you.

29:35.894 --> 29:38.750
But honestly, sir,

29:38.750 --> 29:41.458
the gap you left wasn't as large as we thought.

29:41.458 --> 29:44.285
Especially with Ui Yeong around...

29:54.329 --> 29:58.090
Did you come for work, sir? Or just to browse?

29:58.959 --> 30:01.505
No, about this ring.

30:01.505 --> 30:04.430
Would you do just one final batch?

30:05.230 --> 30:06.770
Couple rings?

30:06.770 --> 30:08.389
Yes.

30:12.292 --> 30:14.208
Well, if you're the one asking,

30:14.208 --> 30:16.213
I can't exactly refuse.

30:17.077 --> 30:20.021
Do you happen to know
your girlfriend's ring size?

30:20.021 --> 30:22.417
I don't have her size. What do I do?

30:22.417 --> 30:25.443
You could just ask her,
or bring a ring she usually has on.

30:25.443 --> 30:28.240
Oh, she does wear rings.
All the time, actually.

30:28.240 --> 30:31.237
So should I sneak one out?

30:31.237 --> 30:34.411
Once the workshop renovation begins,
I won't be able to take orders for a while.

30:34.411 --> 30:37.755
- So you'll need to figure it out quickly.
- Okay, thank you.

30:45.500 --> 30:47.723
Oh, so that's how they do it.

30:49.542 --> 30:51.560
I really like them.

30:53.750 --> 30:55.689
I'm starving.

30:57.375 --> 30:59.568
That's seriously cool.

31:09.000 --> 31:11.948
We should go there sometime.

31:11.948 --> 31:13.525
We should go there later.

31:13.525 --> 31:16.418
I was wondering about that myself.

31:19.499 --> 31:21.917
Oh, is that how they...

31:21.917 --> 31:23.884
Wait one moment.

31:26.590 --> 31:28.585
Oh, yes, Mr. Eun.

31:28.585 --> 31:29.945
Ui Yeong.

31:29.945 --> 31:32.343
- Yes.
- I'm sorry to call at this hour.

31:32.343 --> 31:33.386
Oh, that's alright.

31:33.386 --> 31:35.460
Your friend, you know?

31:35.460 --> 31:36.848
The one whose ceremony is next week.

31:36.848 --> 31:39.080
- Oh, yes, Eun Mi?
- Yes.

31:39.080 --> 31:42.353
Our wedding coordinator heard from her today.

31:42.353 --> 31:45.775
She wanted to know
what the cancellation fee would be.

31:45.775 --> 31:48.420
So did she go ahead and cancel?

31:48.420 --> 31:49.611
No.

31:49.611 --> 31:50.935
When she heard the number,
she sounded startled,

31:50.935 --> 31:53.283
said okay for now, and hung up.

31:53.283 --> 31:56.876
But her voice didn't sound right,

31:56.876 --> 31:59.763
so I thought you should hear about it.

31:59.763 --> 32:03.382
Oh, alright, I appreciate it.

32:04.584 --> 32:07.295
What happened? Your finger... never mind.

32:07.295 --> 32:09.547
Did something happen with your friend?

32:09.547 --> 32:12.764
She called to ask
if canceling the venue was possible.

32:12.764 --> 32:14.136
What?

32:14.136 --> 32:17.133
I think I need to get in touch with her.

32:18.500 --> 32:20.191
What's going on?

32:30.041 --> 32:31.333
- Hello.
- Hello.

32:31.333 --> 32:33.488
- May I have the name on the booking?
- Lee Eun Mi.

32:33.488 --> 32:35.664
- Please follow me.
- Okay.

32:42.337 --> 32:44.317
You're here
for the ceremony gown fitting, right?

32:44.317 --> 32:47.710
Wonderful selection.
It matches your image beautifully.

32:47.710 --> 32:49.750
Let me prepare it
so you can put it on right away.

32:49.750 --> 32:52.132
Oh, no, I'm not the bride.

32:52.132 --> 32:53.876
It's my friend.

32:53.876 --> 32:55.921
- Oh my, I apologize.
- That's okay.

32:55.921 --> 32:59.013
Most brides come by themselves
for the last fitting.

32:59.013 --> 33:00.876
Please sit here and just give me a moment.

33:00.876 --> 33:03.150
Thank you.

33:11.750 --> 33:13.199
I only looked

33:13.199 --> 33:16.080
into what the penalty amount was. That's it.

33:17.584 --> 33:20.134
So there wasn't an actual issue?

33:20.134 --> 33:22.458
It's not so much that anything went wrong.

33:22.458 --> 33:25.584
I always figured marriage was just
what you do when the timing's right.

33:25.584 --> 33:30.417
Finding someone who's as compatible
with me as he is isn't simple either.

33:30.417 --> 33:33.292
But I can't figure out why I'm this uneasy.

33:33.292 --> 33:37.935
I keep asking myself if I can truly commit
my entire life to this person.

33:40.691 --> 33:43.183
With the wedding right around the corner,

33:43.183 --> 33:45.931
your mind must be all over the place.

33:45.931 --> 33:47.478
Oh, I did some reading,

33:47.478 --> 33:50.917
and there's actually something
called pre-wedding blues.

33:56.613 --> 33:58.750
But Eun Mi,

33:58.750 --> 34:00.874
you look absolutely gorgeous.

34:07.169 --> 34:08.208
Yeah.

34:08.208 --> 34:09.960
You have no idea how much weight I dropped.

34:09.960 --> 34:12.189
And how much money I poured into this.

34:12.189 --> 34:14.923
Calling it off
after sending out all those invitations

34:14.923 --> 34:17.683
would embarrass my mom and dad too.

34:18.469 --> 34:20.288
I just have to do this.

34:23.000 --> 34:24.233
Stunning.

34:24.233 --> 34:26.233
Yeah, so much.

34:31.417 --> 34:33.649
[Ui Yeong's Dad]
Is the divorce really set in stone?

34:33.649 --> 34:35.750
There's no room to reconsider?

34:35.750 --> 34:37.445
No. Not at all.

34:37.445 --> 34:41.250
Let's at least spend what's left
of our lives with peace of mind.

34:41.250 --> 34:42.917
Okay.

34:42.917 --> 34:45.169
I'll meet you at the courthouse next week.

34:57.134 --> 34:58.341
I'm back.

34:58.341 --> 34:59.386
Yeah.

34:59.386 --> 35:00.958
Mom, what's all this?

35:00.958 --> 35:03.000
- Are you repotting?
- Yeah.

35:03.000 --> 35:05.265
Catching up on stuff I kept postponing.

35:05.265 --> 35:10.188
I always figured this one was done growing
since it never got any taller.

35:10.188 --> 35:11.625
The roots packed the pot so tight

35:11.625 --> 35:14.315
there was no space left to spread.
So it just stopped.

35:14.315 --> 35:18.570
It figured, this is all I can be in this pot.

35:18.570 --> 35:19.612
Can I help?

35:19.612 --> 35:22.408
No, you'll get soil all over yourself.

35:22.408 --> 35:25.326
Oh, right. I heard from your dad.

35:25.326 --> 35:26.936
Yeah?

35:26.936 --> 35:28.556
What did he say?

35:28.556 --> 35:30.547
He said yes to the divorce.

35:32.167 --> 35:35.094
We're going to the courthouse next week.

35:37.208 --> 35:38.576
Alright.

35:38.576 --> 35:40.072
Noted.

36:00.403 --> 36:03.311
[Wedding toast.txt]

36:06.423 --> 36:09.000
In the storybooks I read growing up,

36:09.000 --> 36:11.876
marriage was always a happy ending.

36:11.876 --> 36:14.834
But now that I've grown up,

36:14.834 --> 36:17.041
I understand why my friend fears

36:17.041 --> 36:20.590
the thought of sharing a lifetime with someone.

36:20.590 --> 36:22.343
And my mother's divorce

36:22.343 --> 36:26.103
feels less like an ending,
and more like taking her life back.

36:26.917 --> 36:28.664
Then

36:28.664 --> 36:32.234
what drives people to choose marriage?

36:37.750 --> 36:38.983
Hello.

36:38.983 --> 36:43.208
My name's Lee Ui Yeong, and I'm a friend
of the bride, Lee Eun Mi.

36:43.208 --> 36:48.242
It's a true privilege to be part

36:48.242 --> 36:50.834
of this special moment for these two.

36:50.834 --> 36:54.089
For both of them to be standing here today...

36:56.834 --> 36:58.722
What are you doing here all of a sudden?

36:58.722 --> 37:00.132
Come on in.

37:00.132 --> 37:02.876
I thought you were joining
the Eat Eat Club, too.

37:02.876 --> 37:06.292
The thing is,
there's a favor I need before we go.

37:06.292 --> 37:07.878
Yes?

37:11.500 --> 37:15.220
So you're planning a secret ring gift,

37:15.220 --> 37:16.565
but you don't have her size.

37:16.565 --> 37:17.743
Right.

37:17.743 --> 37:21.111
I tried checking it on my own,
but it was harder than I thought.

37:21.111 --> 37:22.557
Could you find out on my behalf?

37:22.557 --> 37:25.579
Just naturally, so she doesn't catch on?

37:27.792 --> 37:31.285
Hold on, is this about that thing
young couples do nowadays?

37:31.285 --> 37:33.413
Like a proposal or something?

37:33.413 --> 37:35.164
Oh, no. Nothing like that.

37:35.164 --> 37:36.343
Why not?

37:36.343 --> 37:39.101
Don't you think it's time for marriage?

37:39.101 --> 37:41.802
Well... it's always been on my mind.

37:41.802 --> 37:44.375
But it isn't something I can decide by myself,

37:44.375 --> 37:47.009
so I'm waiting for Ui Yeong

37:47.009 --> 37:48.346
to feel that way in her own time.

37:48.346 --> 37:49.598
Don't worry about it.

37:49.598 --> 37:51.558
I've been your matchmaker
from the start, haven't I?

37:51.558 --> 37:52.934
Leave it to me.

37:52.934 --> 37:56.458
I'll see to it you're both wearing rings.

37:56.458 --> 37:57.959
Okay.

38:07.113 --> 38:09.132
- Help yourselves.
- I'll ladle out some soup, too.

38:09.132 --> 38:11.834
This is called gon.
It's incredibly hard to come by.

38:11.834 --> 38:13.796
Okay then, let me handle this one myself.

38:13.796 --> 38:15.336
Oh right, the alcohol.

38:15.336 --> 38:17.110
Tae Seop.

38:17.110 --> 38:19.709
My mom covered the drinks for tonight.

38:19.709 --> 38:21.087
Pour whatever you want.

38:21.087 --> 38:22.876
The owner already said it's fine.

38:22.876 --> 38:24.495
- Great selection.
- Yeah.

38:24.495 --> 38:26.709
- Then let's open with the pricey ones first.
- Sounds good.

38:26.709 --> 38:27.884
I'll just use soju glasses for pouring.

38:27.884 --> 38:28.678
- Sure.
- Okay.

38:28.678 --> 38:30.470
Give our thanks to your mother.

38:30.470 --> 38:32.513
Of course. My mom's been

38:32.513 --> 38:34.265
focusing on her wellness these days.

38:34.265 --> 38:35.641
Oh, that reminds me, Seung Jun,

38:35.641 --> 38:37.852
book me and my mom for 10 PT sessions.

38:37.852 --> 38:39.333
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

38:39.333 --> 38:41.125
Then sign me up for 20.

38:41.125 --> 38:43.617
- Working out together would be a blast.
- That would be great.

38:44.650 --> 38:45.709
- Thank you.
- Oh, sure.

38:45.709 --> 38:48.709
I'll add three complimentary sessions
for each of you.

38:48.709 --> 38:50.542
Love it.

38:50.542 --> 38:52.702
Where's Sae Byeok, by the way?

38:52.702 --> 38:55.028
She booked a show she couldn't get a refund on,

38:55.028 --> 38:56.333
so she couldn't come.

38:56.333 --> 38:58.664
She's probably too caught up
in her workplace romance.

38:58.664 --> 39:00.098
- Adorable.
- Really?

39:00.098 --> 39:03.343
Well, since everyone's gathered,
there's something I should share.

39:04.086 --> 39:06.966
Actually, I'll be leaving the hotel soon

39:06.966 --> 39:08.375
and heading overseas.

39:08.375 --> 39:10.539
Wait, just like that?

39:10.539 --> 39:11.959
Where to?

39:11.959 --> 39:16.010
I got the head chef position
at a fusion Korean restaurant in New York.

39:16.838 --> 39:20.542
I wanted to let you all know
before we really got into the food.

39:20.542 --> 39:21.976
That's incredible. Congratulations.

39:21.976 --> 39:23.556
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

39:23.556 --> 39:24.693
Congratulations.

39:24.693 --> 39:27.375
But couldn't you stick around just a bit more?

39:27.375 --> 39:28.834
- Mr. Eun,
- Yes?

39:28.834 --> 39:31.176
you're really letting someone this talented go?

39:31.176 --> 39:34.136
When someone's this determined, what can I do?

39:34.136 --> 39:37.116
People in this field don't stick around
one spot for long.

39:37.116 --> 39:40.584
You keep heading
to wherever pushes you further.

39:40.584 --> 39:44.667
But thanks to you all,
I've tasted chicken feet,

39:44.667 --> 39:48.541
sea pineapple, sundae,
and even this fresh cod stew.

39:48.541 --> 39:50.876
I'm leaving with so much inspiration.

39:50.876 --> 39:54.780
Sounds like the Eat Eat Club
really earned its keep.

39:54.780 --> 39:56.964
Alright then, let's have a drink!

39:56.964 --> 39:58.208
Cheers!

39:58.208 --> 39:59.850
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

39:59.850 --> 40:01.405
- Safe travels.
- Tonight's my treat.

40:01.405 --> 40:02.937
- Oh, really?
- Awesome.

40:02.937 --> 40:06.000
- Thank you for treating us.
- Thank you.

40:06.000 --> 40:07.441
With cod,

40:07.441 --> 40:10.619
all they know out west is frying it.

40:11.827 --> 40:14.250
But this broth is out of this world.

40:14.250 --> 40:16.993
One sip of this
and you won't be able to forget us.

40:16.993 --> 40:18.417
I won't forget.

40:18.417 --> 40:19.456
No chance I could.

40:19.456 --> 40:21.238
- Delicious, right?
- Yeah.

40:25.041 --> 40:28.516
While we're all together,
I have a little question myself.

40:28.516 --> 40:29.915
What's that?

40:29.915 --> 40:31.236
So...

40:31.236 --> 40:37.195
I'm looking to get my wife a ring as a present.

40:37.195 --> 40:39.465
What size ring does Ui Yeong wear?

40:39.465 --> 40:41.456
Me?

40:41.456 --> 40:44.292
Hold on, you're shopping for your wife's ring.

40:44.292 --> 40:47.614
Why do you need Ui Yeong's size?

40:50.680 --> 40:51.701
Well...

40:51.701 --> 40:54.238
It's because her hands are
about the same as Ui Yeong's.

40:54.238 --> 40:56.034
Oh, is that so?

40:56.034 --> 40:58.709
- Oh, well my ring size...
- Yeah.

41:01.736 --> 41:03.458
I honestly have no idea.

41:03.458 --> 41:05.256
I bet nobody does. Do you know yours?

41:05.256 --> 41:06.625
Small?

41:06.625 --> 41:08.736
Then mine's extra small!

41:08.736 --> 41:10.458
- No clue about mine either.
- Right?

41:10.458 --> 41:12.798
- So nobody knows.
- Oh, I'm sorry.

41:12.798 --> 41:16.500
No, don't be. Well, this is a pickle.

41:16.500 --> 41:19.957
I really thought you'd be the one person
who'd know your wife's ring size.

41:19.957 --> 41:21.877
You're always so attentive.

41:21.877 --> 41:23.937
Honey, let's make a point
of knowing from now on.

41:23.937 --> 41:25.863
Left ring finger.

41:25.863 --> 41:26.877
Thanks.

41:26.877 --> 41:28.375
Go ahead, take the ring.

41:28.375 --> 41:30.238
Thank you.

41:30.238 --> 41:34.703
I've let a lot of people down tonight.
Myself included.

41:35.625 --> 41:37.664
Come on.

41:38.917 --> 41:41.458
With all this fancy liquor sitting right here,

41:41.458 --> 41:43.628
all I'm craving is soju.

41:46.208 --> 41:48.125
Let me pour you one.

41:48.125 --> 41:49.968
Sure.

41:50.917 --> 41:53.013
Nice and slow.

42:07.125 --> 42:08.740
Ui Yeong.

42:08.740 --> 42:12.750
I went to the courthouse
with your mom to file the divorce papers,

42:12.750 --> 42:15.361
and now I'm heading home.

42:15.361 --> 42:18.458
I know this has weighed on you because of me.

42:18.458 --> 42:21.750
Once everything's sorted,
let's meet up, just us.

42:42.564 --> 42:45.106
Rice balls, coming right up!

42:45.876 --> 42:47.125
Welcome!

42:47.125 --> 42:48.445
Do you do takeout?

42:48.445 --> 42:49.750
- Absolutely!
- Sure.

42:49.750 --> 42:51.265
How many are you ordering for?

42:51.265 --> 42:52.325
- Two.
- Two?

42:52.325 --> 42:54.108
I'll do medium size then.

42:54.108 --> 42:55.151
Two medium for takeout.

42:55.151 --> 42:57.805
Actually, go ahead and wait upstairs
on the second floor.

42:57.805 --> 42:59.544
- I'll have them up to you in no time.
- Okay.

42:59.544 --> 43:02.207
Honey, two medium for takeout!

43:06.208 --> 43:09.290
Rice balls, here we go!

43:09.290 --> 43:11.465
[We're all someone's treasure]

43:16.331 --> 43:19.417
- Our son hung that up.
- Oh, I see.

43:19.417 --> 43:21.969
We're all so caught up
getting tossed around by life,

43:21.969 --> 43:23.372
we lose sight of things like this.

43:23.372 --> 43:25.542
At least while eating these chicken feet,

43:25.542 --> 43:28.031
I want customers to know they matter.

43:28.031 --> 43:29.479
This is complimentary.

43:29.479 --> 43:32.208
- Thank you.
- Sure.

43:32.208 --> 43:35.477
I think your son is

43:35.477 --> 43:38.463
reminding the customers to be kind to you

43:38.463 --> 43:41.410
because you mean the world to him.

43:43.034 --> 43:45.184
You really think so?

43:45.184 --> 43:48.000
Our boy really does have a heart

43:48.000 --> 43:51.874
that's just impossibly deep.

43:51.874 --> 43:54.410
But you haven't been here before, have you?

43:54.410 --> 43:55.920
- Yes, this is my first visit.
- Sure.

43:55.920 --> 43:58.041
My daughter absolutely loves your chicken feet.

43:58.041 --> 44:01.017
- So your daughter's been a regular all along!
- Yeah.

44:01.017 --> 44:02.292
She has

44:02.292 --> 44:05.348
- a real knack for spotting quality.
- Sure.

44:05.348 --> 44:07.660
From the ingredients to the taste,

44:07.660 --> 44:09.917
she just knows when something's right.

44:09.917 --> 44:11.649
Let me think now...

44:11.649 --> 44:13.834
I remember the faces

44:13.834 --> 44:16.524
of just about every regular we have.

44:16.524 --> 44:18.317
Oh... looking at you closely,

44:18.317 --> 44:21.876
the way the corners of your mouth lift

44:21.876 --> 44:23.722
when you smile, right around here...

44:23.722 --> 44:27.108
No, I'm sorry, no matter how hard I try,
I can't figure it out.

44:28.584 --> 44:30.242
I'll bring my daughter along next time.

44:30.242 --> 44:33.582
Oh please do. When you bring her with you,

44:33.582 --> 44:37.086
the steamed egg, the rice,
all of it's complimentary.

44:37.086 --> 44:38.122
Thank you.

44:38.122 --> 44:41.014
- Hang on just a bit.
- Thank you.

44:42.958 --> 44:44.790
That looks amazing.

44:46.258 --> 44:50.041
Oh, today was the day
your parents went to the courthouse.

44:50.041 --> 44:51.475
Yeah.

44:51.475 --> 44:53.397
I considered going along,

44:53.397 --> 44:56.834
but it felt like they wanted
to settle it on their own, peacefully.

44:56.834 --> 44:58.018
That was the right call.

44:58.018 --> 45:00.218
Tae Seop, that chair you made?

45:00.218 --> 45:02.419
- I'm in it right now.
- Yeah.

45:02.419 --> 45:04.250
Is anything bothering you?

45:04.250 --> 45:05.398
No.

45:05.398 --> 45:06.958
Quite the opposite.

45:06.958 --> 45:11.876
I mean, here I am, even discussing
my parents' divorce with total ease.

45:11.876 --> 45:13.497
Well...

45:13.497 --> 45:15.327
there's actually a little trick to it.

45:15.327 --> 45:16.667
Oh, what's that?

45:16.667 --> 45:20.709
I set the backrest at about seven degrees.
Just the faintest lean.

45:20.709 --> 45:23.593
It's only a tiny angle,
but it feels comfortable, doesn't it?

45:23.593 --> 45:25.713
Yes, completely.

45:25.713 --> 45:29.597
I'm always tilted a little
in your direction, too.

45:29.597 --> 45:31.673
So anytime you need to, just rest against me.

45:31.673 --> 45:33.475
Okay.

45:33.475 --> 45:34.874
Oh? Mom's back.

45:34.874 --> 45:36.014
Let me call you later.

45:36.014 --> 45:37.229
Oh, sure.

45:37.229 --> 45:38.493
Mom, you're back?

45:38.493 --> 45:40.041
Yeah.

45:40.041 --> 45:41.313
What's that?

45:41.313 --> 45:43.069
- You didn't eat yet, did you?
- No.

45:43.069 --> 45:44.667
- I picked up something you love.
- What is it?

45:44.667 --> 45:45.738
[Songi Spicy Chicken Feet]

45:46.333 --> 45:49.040
- Songi Spicy Chicken Feet?
- Yeah.

45:53.391 --> 45:55.347
So the woman I met today

45:55.347 --> 45:56.916
is Tae Seop's mom?

45:56.916 --> 45:58.125
Yeah.

45:58.125 --> 46:00.349
You can't imagine
how stunned I was when I realized.

46:00.349 --> 46:02.119
Isn't that wild?

46:03.041 --> 46:05.859
Does being sweet
run in the family or something?

46:06.528 --> 46:08.041
While I was sitting there today,

46:08.041 --> 46:10.584
she brought me a Sprite as a freebie.

46:10.584 --> 46:12.647
- She did?
- Yeah.

46:20.500 --> 46:22.233
Mom,

46:22.233 --> 46:25.285
at the courthouse today with Dad,
nothing happened, right?

46:27.571 --> 46:30.366
It was fine. Over in no time.

46:30.366 --> 46:33.285
They said we need to come back
one more time in a month.

46:33.285 --> 46:35.013
I can't believe I put this off for so long

46:35.013 --> 46:37.338
when it feels this freeing.

46:39.917 --> 46:41.208
Hey, Mom.

46:41.208 --> 46:42.255
Yeah?

46:42.255 --> 46:46.139
If you had another life,
you wouldn't tie the knot, right?

46:48.008 --> 46:49.286
I think I still would.

46:49.286 --> 46:51.083
You would?

46:51.083 --> 46:54.431
I mean, sure, it turned out this way,

46:54.431 --> 46:55.849
but at the time,

46:55.849 --> 46:58.625
it was the best call I could make.

46:58.625 --> 47:00.562
So even if I could go back,

47:00.562 --> 47:02.864
I think I'd choose the same thing.

47:03.792 --> 47:06.645
What if you returned
knowing everything you know now?

47:06.645 --> 47:09.265
Oh, you know how everyone
loves those hypotheticals.

47:09.265 --> 47:11.826
Then I'd fight even harder
to live the very same life.

47:11.826 --> 47:14.083
Because that's the only way
I'd end up with you.

47:14.083 --> 47:15.213
What?

47:15.213 --> 47:16.993
Just to bring me into this world?

47:17.793 --> 47:19.501
Everything gets thrown your way,

47:19.501 --> 47:22.087
but it's a good time, isn't it? Being alive.

47:22.087 --> 47:25.762
And having you here
makes me a little less alone.

47:30.092 --> 47:32.672
Now that I've got my freedom,
I should soak it in.

47:32.672 --> 47:35.764
Maybe I'll use some vacation days
and go somewhere.

47:35.764 --> 47:37.041
Pick up a new language too.

47:37.041 --> 47:41.312
I've always had my eye on Spanish.

47:41.312 --> 47:42.638
Should we learn together and go?

47:42.638 --> 47:43.737
Oh, Mom.

47:43.737 --> 47:45.775
What if we set up a travel savings fund?

47:45.775 --> 47:47.917
- Oh, that sounds nice.
- Right?

47:47.917 --> 47:49.375
You cover 70, I'll handle 30.

47:49.375 --> 47:50.615
Oh, please.

47:50.615 --> 47:52.997
You're starting to sound
like an evil stepmother.

48:12.000 --> 48:13.545
How do I look? Is it alright?

48:13.545 --> 48:14.745
Alright? Are you serious?

48:14.745 --> 48:17.500
You look like an angel right now.

48:17.500 --> 48:20.312
I've been warming up my mouth muscles
nonstop for the toast.

48:20.312 --> 48:23.025
You'll need to smile a ton,
so get those facial muscles relaxed now,

48:23.025 --> 48:24.802
okay?

48:26.792 --> 48:28.584
- You're here?
- You're here?

48:28.584 --> 48:29.870
Hi.

48:29.870 --> 48:30.903
Hurry, get a photo.

48:30.903 --> 48:32.954
- Take a seat.
- You're so pretty.

48:35.346 --> 48:36.375
Hey.

48:36.375 --> 48:38.917
She is the star today. The star.

48:38.917 --> 48:40.962
I'm so nervous.

48:43.832 --> 48:44.834
[Bride's Side]

48:44.834 --> 48:47.135
Thank you for coming.

48:50.917 --> 48:52.219
It's been so long.

48:52.219 --> 48:55.417
- Look at this little trooper.
- You've gotten so big.

48:55.417 --> 48:56.512
It's been a while.

48:56.512 --> 48:59.125
- Don't they look so happy?
- The dress looks perfect on her.

48:59.125 --> 49:00.584
- Right? It suits her so well.
- Right?

49:00.584 --> 49:02.918
- Like a princess.
- She really does look happy, doesn't she?

49:02.918 --> 49:04.189
- Right?
- No thoughts about getting married?

49:04.189 --> 49:06.279
- Oh, stop.
- Quit it.

49:07.208 --> 49:08.480
Ui Yeong.

49:08.480 --> 49:09.834
Oh? You're here?

49:09.834 --> 49:11.584
He's my boyfriend.

49:11.584 --> 49:12.750
- What?
- No way.

49:12.750 --> 49:14.792
- Your boyfriend is so handsome.
- Really?

49:14.792 --> 49:16.072
You really met on a blind date?

49:16.072 --> 49:18.742
You've got skills.

49:18.742 --> 49:19.752
Say hello.

49:19.752 --> 49:21.292
Hello. I'm Song Tae Seop.

49:21.292 --> 49:22.412
- Hello.
- Hello.

49:22.412 --> 49:24.132
We went to college with Ui Yeong.

49:24.132 --> 49:25.952
She's told me a lot about you.

49:25.952 --> 49:29.420
Oh, really? You two look so good together.

49:29.420 --> 49:31.041
- You think?
- Let's all get together

49:31.041 --> 49:32.472
with our partners next time.

49:32.472 --> 49:34.112
Sure, sounds great. Call us anytime.

49:34.112 --> 49:36.167
Oh, okay.

49:36.167 --> 49:37.292
- What?
- Let's head in.

49:37.292 --> 49:38.792
- Should we start heading in?
- Yeah, sure.

49:38.792 --> 49:39.834
- We'll go in first.
- See you inside.

49:39.834 --> 49:41.958
- See you soon.
- Okay.

49:41.958 --> 49:43.699
He's incredibly handsome.

49:43.699 --> 49:45.709
Excuse me.

49:45.709 --> 49:47.375
You're the bride's friend, right?

49:47.375 --> 49:49.442
Yes, I am.

49:49.442 --> 49:52.208
Is something wrong?

49:52.208 --> 49:55.782
The bride won't come out.

49:55.782 --> 49:57.114
What?

49:57.114 --> 49:59.624
She says she won't come out.

50:02.625 --> 50:04.504
Could you please...

50:06.876 --> 50:08.224
This way.

50:08.224 --> 50:10.625
She asked to be left alone, so I came out,

50:10.625 --> 50:13.764
but she's bolted the door and isn't answering.

50:13.764 --> 50:17.144
Should I ask the manager for the key?

50:17.144 --> 50:18.204
No.

50:18.204 --> 50:20.750
Let me try speaking with her.

50:20.750 --> 50:22.230
Okay.

50:23.852 --> 50:25.184
Ui Yeong.

50:25.184 --> 50:27.777
- I'll wait right out here.
- Okay.

50:33.709 --> 50:35.155
Eun Mi.

50:35.155 --> 50:36.911
It's me.

50:38.996 --> 50:40.376
Ui Yeong?

50:40.376 --> 50:41.556
Yeah.

50:41.556 --> 50:44.542
Are you alright? Does something hurt?

50:44.542 --> 50:47.918
My heart's racing
and I feel like I might be sick.

50:47.918 --> 50:50.876
And this dress feels like it's strangling me.

50:50.876 --> 50:52.500
I did some research,

50:52.500 --> 50:54.542
and supposedly calling it off
before I walk in is still better

50:54.542 --> 50:56.041
than paying a fortune in damages afterward.

50:56.041 --> 50:57.925
Listen,

50:57.925 --> 51:01.389
just quit overthinking for now.

51:01.389 --> 51:04.309
If you can manage it,
will you try unlocking the door?

51:04.309 --> 51:06.441
I'm alone out here.

51:09.911 --> 51:11.696
Eun Mi.

51:15.292 --> 51:17.035
Eun Mi.

51:19.458 --> 51:21.990
It's fine.

51:21.990 --> 51:23.791
Feeling nervous is totally normal.

51:23.791 --> 51:25.918
Being frightened is normal too.

51:27.083 --> 51:29.250
But

51:29.250 --> 51:31.833
fearing marriage

51:31.833 --> 51:35.041
and questioning
whether this person is right for you

51:35.041 --> 51:36.971
are two separate things.

51:38.375 --> 51:40.137
Can you

51:40.137 --> 51:43.478
honestly say there wasn't one moment
that made you feel sure?

51:51.917 --> 51:53.654
Ho Jin.

51:55.083 --> 51:56.567
Are you okay?

51:56.567 --> 52:00.292
Oh no, she really has to walk in now.

52:00.292 --> 52:01.616
It's fine.

52:01.616 --> 52:04.707
Running a bit behind won't ruin anything.

52:12.163 --> 52:14.008
It's been tough, hasn't it?

52:21.041 --> 52:23.625
In that stiff dress all day,

52:23.625 --> 52:26.391
unable to let on how you really feel.

52:26.391 --> 52:27.681
Eun Mi.

52:27.681 --> 52:29.703
If it's too much,
you don't have to walk in there.

52:29.703 --> 52:31.536
It's fine.

52:33.041 --> 52:34.774
Ho Jin.

52:34.774 --> 52:36.450
It's fine.

52:37.375 --> 52:40.284
I'll always be right here next to you.

52:42.824 --> 52:44.466
Okay?

52:54.941 --> 52:57.218
I'll go in.

52:59.208 --> 53:01.180
I'll go in.

53:04.927 --> 53:05.941
Hello, everyone.

53:05.941 --> 53:08.055
My name's Yoo Jeong Hwa,

53:08.055 --> 53:12.309
a friend of the groom, Jung Ho Jin,
and I'll be hosting today's ceremony.

53:12.309 --> 53:13.393
Even with your packed schedules,

53:13.393 --> 53:15.604
we truly appreciate every family member

53:15.604 --> 53:18.489
and guest who came to celebrate this union.

53:18.489 --> 53:20.667
- What's wrong?
- On behalf of both families,

53:20.667 --> 53:24.783
- we offer our heartfelt gratitude once more.
- I think my toast was too naive.

53:24.783 --> 53:27.645
I wrote it like everything was
sunshine and roses.

53:28.370 --> 53:29.529
Then

53:29.529 --> 53:31.483
just follow your heart.

53:31.483 --> 53:33.705
- If it's honest, it'll matter no matter what.
- We will now commence

53:33.705 --> 53:35.709
the wedding ceremony

53:35.709 --> 53:38.130
of Jung Ho Jin and Lee Eun Mi.

53:38.130 --> 53:41.250
Please turn your attention to the rear.

53:41.250 --> 53:43.674
With your blessings, today's stars,

53:43.674 --> 53:45.990
the bride and groom,
will now make their entrance.

53:45.990 --> 53:48.223
Bride and groom,

53:48.223 --> 53:49.923
please proceed.

53:51.690 --> 53:53.691
Let us greet them
with a warm round of applause,

53:53.691 --> 53:56.527
celebrating the future awaiting these two.

53:58.171 --> 54:02.731
Friends of the couple,
let's get a little louder.

54:02.731 --> 54:05.737
The two of them are holding hands,

54:05.737 --> 54:08.083
stepping calmly forward

54:08.083 --> 54:10.471
toward their shared future together.

54:10.471 --> 54:13.083
Today, through the covenant of marriage,

54:13.083 --> 54:17.111
they have pledged
to walk a lifetime side by side.

54:17.111 --> 54:18.959
This is a vow to love each other,

54:18.959 --> 54:22.713
to uphold and care for one another

54:22.713 --> 54:28.041
through illness and grief,
through joy and happiness...

54:28.041 --> 54:29.848
We will now hear

54:29.848 --> 54:33.083
a toast from a friend of the bride.

54:33.083 --> 54:34.919
I'll be right back.

54:48.489 --> 54:49.791
[Hi everyone, I'm Lee Ui Yeong,
a close friend of the bride, Lee Eun Mi]

54:49.791 --> 54:51.040
[I am truly honored to be part of
this beautiful beginning for the two of them]

55:00.041 --> 55:01.577
Hello.

55:01.577 --> 55:04.845
I'm the friend's bride...

55:06.417 --> 55:10.434
No, a friend of the bride, Lee Ui Yeong.

55:14.834 --> 55:18.100
I'm trembling so much right now,

55:18.100 --> 55:21.292
but the two people
who must be trembling even more

55:21.292 --> 55:24.917
are the bride and groom right in front of me.

55:24.917 --> 55:29.145
When you step out of here
once today's ceremony ends,

55:29.145 --> 55:32.115
you might feel as though your whole life

55:32.115 --> 55:34.326
has just shifted.

55:34.326 --> 55:36.208
[Third Act Company, Meeting with the Cast]

55:36.208 --> 55:38.292
Take your time and read through this.

55:38.292 --> 55:39.706
Okay.

55:39.706 --> 55:42.474
[Third Act Company Actor Contract]

55:42.474 --> 55:44.417
The reason we hold back

55:44.417 --> 55:46.995
before major decisions is

55:46.995 --> 55:49.507
because we can't tell

55:49.507 --> 55:51.876
where today's choice

55:51.876 --> 55:53.720
will lead us.

55:53.720 --> 55:56.307
[Shin Ji Su]

56:05.792 --> 56:08.167
Which doors will open,

56:08.167 --> 56:11.924
and which possibilities will shut.

56:11.924 --> 56:12.958
Yeah.

56:12.958 --> 56:14.292
The last scene hit a bit of a delay...

56:14.292 --> 56:18.159
What waits at the end of that road,

56:18.159 --> 56:19.913
nobody can tell

56:19.913 --> 56:21.007
[Watching Son Jeong A work on set,
she was remarkable]

56:21.007 --> 56:23.466
until they walk it for themselves.

56:24.668 --> 56:25.794
[What was it like performing with her?]

56:25.794 --> 56:27.416
[I took away so much and would love
to collaborate with her on another project]

56:32.041 --> 56:35.208
To weather the uncertainty of life,

56:35.208 --> 56:38.640
we keep calculating,

56:38.640 --> 56:41.834
picture every what-if,

56:41.834 --> 56:43.041
and sometimes

56:43.041 --> 56:46.614
just decide to stay hopeful.

56:52.500 --> 56:53.688
Peekaboo.

56:53.688 --> 56:55.876
In the end, maybe life is

56:55.876 --> 56:58.159
just figuring out

56:58.159 --> 57:00.120
how to take one step forward,

57:00.120 --> 57:03.214
even when nothing is guaranteed.

57:04.709 --> 57:09.303
I believe marriage is no different.

57:10.917 --> 57:13.125
The path you share

57:13.125 --> 57:15.528
won't always be easy.

57:15.528 --> 57:18.667
There'll be painful days
just as often as joyful ones,

57:18.667 --> 57:23.911
and there will surely
be moments you never expected.

57:23.911 --> 57:26.375
But even so,

57:26.375 --> 57:27.947
if you trust in each other

57:27.947 --> 57:31.242
and want to take on whatever lies ahead,

57:32.027 --> 57:35.165
and if you want to
step into an uncertain future

57:35.165 --> 57:37.125
side by side,

57:37.125 --> 57:39.284
then I want to root for the bravery

57:39.284 --> 57:42.167
of these two people

57:42.167 --> 57:44.131
with all my heart, until the very end.

57:44.131 --> 57:45.572
Congratulations on your wedding.

57:45.572 --> 57:47.466
Congratulations.

57:59.167 --> 58:01.685
Bride and groom,

58:01.685 --> 58:03.245
march!

58:03.245 --> 58:05.734
A warm round of applause, please.

58:45.792 --> 58:48.060
Today was quite a day, wasn't it?

58:48.060 --> 58:49.420
Yeah.

58:49.420 --> 58:51.904
The bride was in tears one second
and smiling the next.

58:51.904 --> 58:54.894
It really struck me
that marriage is such a monumental thing.

58:55.697 --> 58:57.125
It felt

58:57.125 --> 59:00.498
like I was the one seeing my friend off.

59:03.827 --> 59:05.036
That's no small feat.

59:05.036 --> 59:06.095
Yeah.

59:06.095 --> 59:08.584
How about a stroll before we head back?

59:08.584 --> 59:10.211
Sure.

59:16.333 --> 59:17.607
So

59:17.607 --> 59:20.435
what was in the original toast
you planned to read?

59:20.435 --> 59:23.433
Eun Mi specifically asked me to prepare a toast

59:23.433 --> 59:26.323
that wouldn't bring anyone to tears.

59:26.323 --> 59:28.685
So I went with a purely statistical angle.

59:28.685 --> 59:29.709
What?

59:29.709 --> 59:31.743
- Want to hear it?
- Yes.

59:31.743 --> 59:33.792
Out of 50 million people in our country,

59:33.792 --> 59:35.900
15 million are single.

59:35.900 --> 59:38.784
Half of them are men, so that's 7.5 million.

59:38.784 --> 59:42.625
If you figure 90 percent are heterosexual,
that's 6.8 million.

59:42.625 --> 59:43.876
Out of all those people,

59:43.876 --> 59:48.083
what are the chances of meeting one man
and falling in love?

59:48.083 --> 59:50.503
- Astronomically slim.
- Exactly.

59:50.503 --> 59:52.703
That's what I put down.

59:52.703 --> 59:56.053
That the two of them meeting
and falling in love is already a miracle.

01:00:00.167 --> 01:00:02.251
Oh, there's something I want to give you.

01:00:02.251 --> 01:00:04.103
What is it?

01:00:17.000 --> 01:00:18.291
It's gorgeous.

01:00:18.291 --> 01:00:21.905
The moment I first laid eyes on it,
I wanted it to be yours.

01:00:21.905 --> 01:00:26.083
Figuring out your ring size
was a bit tricky, though.

01:00:26.083 --> 01:00:28.627
But then how did you figure it out?

01:00:31.208 --> 01:00:33.292
Thank you.

01:00:33.292 --> 01:00:34.584
Want to come along?

01:00:34.584 --> 01:00:37.103
Sure. Take me with you.

01:00:37.103 --> 01:00:39.798
Sign me up as an option.

01:00:39.798 --> 01:00:44.059
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

01:00:46.876 --> 01:00:49.269
We really drank a lot.

01:00:49.269 --> 01:00:51.500
- It actually looks legit.
- Ui Yeong, I love you.

01:00:51.500 --> 01:00:54.062
I love you too.

01:00:54.062 --> 01:00:55.271
Chef, I love you.

01:00:55.271 --> 01:00:57.208
I love you too.

01:00:57.208 --> 01:01:00.377
- You have to come back.
- Tae Seop, I love you so much.

01:01:06.917 --> 01:01:08.569
Hello.

01:01:08.569 --> 01:01:10.262
- Oh, hello.
- Yes.

01:01:11.097 --> 01:01:12.389
You finally found out the size?

01:01:12.389 --> 01:01:13.543
Yes.

01:01:20.887 --> 01:01:23.083
That's the size.

01:01:23.083 --> 01:01:25.434
This is the size?

01:01:32.834 --> 01:01:35.402
Let me have your hand. I'll slide it on.

01:01:52.290 --> 01:01:54.153
Is this it?

01:01:56.416 --> 01:01:59.089
The moment my friends kept telling me about?

01:02:14.125 --> 01:02:15.778
Look.

01:02:17.607 --> 01:02:19.469
How is it?

01:02:22.934 --> 01:02:24.458
Tae Seop.

01:02:24.458 --> 01:02:26.057
Yes.

01:02:31.167 --> 01:02:34.542
It's not just that I like you.

01:02:34.542 --> 01:02:37.500
I love you. A lot.

01:02:37.500 --> 01:02:39.167
How do you always know

01:02:39.167 --> 01:02:41.328
what I need before I even say it?

01:02:41.328 --> 01:02:43.667
Because I'm paying attention to you.

01:02:43.667 --> 01:02:44.756
Me?

01:02:44.756 --> 01:02:45.970
Her boyfriend.

01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:47.509
This is a drilling machine.

01:02:47.509 --> 01:02:48.448
I'm calling the police.

01:02:48.448 --> 01:02:50.375
- Three!
- Three.

01:02:50.375 --> 01:02:51.635
Hi, Sae Byeok.

01:02:51.635 --> 01:02:54.835
We'll build our love in our own way.

01:02:54.835 --> 01:02:57.958
I came because I missed you.

01:02:57.958 --> 01:03:00.946
I'm glad we found each other when we did.

01:03:05.113 --> 01:03:06.823
I like you, Ui Yeong.

01:03:06.823 --> 01:03:09.530
I like you too, Tae Seop.

01:03:09.530 --> 01:03:12.086
You can't fall asleep here.

01:03:21.881 --> 01:03:23.834
Tae Seop.

01:03:23.834 --> 01:03:26.458
Thank you for coming to find me.

01:03:26.458 --> 01:03:27.500
Oh my!

01:03:27.500 --> 01:03:29.276
I'm sorry.

01:03:33.292 --> 01:03:36.041
Hello. I'm Song Tae Seop.

01:03:36.041 --> 01:03:38.192
I'm Lee Ui Yeong.

01:03:41.083 --> 01:03:43.682
Do you agree

01:03:43.682 --> 01:03:45.917
to a relationship

01:03:45.917 --> 01:03:47.868
with the intention of marriage?

01:03:49.616 --> 01:03:51.041
Tae Seop.

01:03:51.041 --> 01:03:52.639
Yes.

01:03:53.251 --> 01:03:54.958
Do you agree

01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:59.250
to a relationship with me,

01:03:59.250 --> 01:04:01.321
with the intention of marriage?

01:04:13.014 --> 01:04:14.686
Yes.

01:04:57.930 --> 01:05:02.055
[A woman who picks love]

01:05:03.019 --> 01:05:06.151
[A man who feels like the answer]

01:05:07.106 --> 01:05:10.355
[A man who shifts everything]

01:05:11.152 --> 01:05:12.278
[45cm]

01:05:12.278 --> 01:05:15.448
[0cm]

01:05:15.448 --> 01:05:20.661
[Hello, I'm Shin Ji Su]

01:05:20.661 --> 01:05:24.165
[Seung Jun and Hyun Min]

01:05:24.165 --> 01:05:29.027
[Purchase complete. Purchasing Team]

01:05:29.962 --> 01:05:34.175
[Don't panic. Don't be surprised. HOME]

01:05:34.175 --> 01:05:38.304
[Queen of Romance]

01:05:38.304 --> 01:05:42.027
[No one but Mom. No one but you]

01:05:42.725 --> 01:05:46.145
[We're all someone's treasure]

01:05:46.145 --> 01:05:50.775
[Looking forward to your growth]

01:05:50.775 --> 01:05:55.613
[Office study group. Eat Eat Club FOREVER]

01:05:55.613 --> 01:05:59.534
[It's not because of you, but thanks to you]

01:05:59.534 --> 01:06:04.288
[Theater Company, Act Two]

01:06:04.288 --> 01:06:08.075
[A bond from the past]

01:06:09.001 --> 01:06:12.880
[A bond to treasure]

01:06:12.880 --> 01:06:16.786
[A bond let go]

01:06:18.052 --> 01:06:22.140
[A nightmare of a bond]

01:06:22.140 --> 01:06:26.739
[Marriage...?]

01:06:52.378 --> 01:06:58.335
[Do you agree to date with marriage in mind?]
